{"tool_name":"abaenrichment","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"abaenrichment","home":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/ABAEnrichment.html","license":"GPL-2.0","summary":"The package is designed to test for enrichment of user defined candidate genes in the set of expressed genes in different human brain regions. The core function 'aba_enrich' integrates the expression of the candidate gene set (averaged across donors) and the structural information of the brain using an ontology, both provided by the Allen Brain Atlas project. 'aba_enrich' interfaces the ontology enrichment software FUNC to perform the statistical analyses.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T15:03:07Z","last_update_date":"2019-01-13T17:01:58Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.4.0"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:abaenrichment","credit":[{"email":"steffi_grote@eva.mpg.de","name":"Steffi Grote","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/ABAEnrichment.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Gene-set enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2436"}]}],"name":"ABAEnrichment","operating_system":["Mac","Windows"],"owner":"bioconductor_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw392","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 The Author 2016.Summary: We present ABAEnrichment, an R package that tests for expression enrichment in specific brain regions at different developmental stages using expression information gathered from multiple regions of the adult and developing human brain, together with ontologically organized structural information about the brain, both provided by the Allen Brain Atlas. We validate ABAEnrichment by successfully recovering the origin of gene sets identified in specific brain cell-types and developmental stages.","authors":[{"name":"Dannemann M."},{"name":"Grote S."},{"name":"Kelso J."},{"name":"Prufer K."}],"citationCount":14,"date":"2016-10-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"ABAEnrichment: An R package to test for gene set expression enrichment in the adult and developing human brain"},"pmcid":"PMC5048072","pmid":"27354695","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene expression","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0203"},{"term":"Neurobiology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3304"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"ABAEnrichment","home":"https://bio.tools/abaenrichment","license":"GPL-2.0","version":"1.4.0","summary":"The package is designed to test for enrichment of user defined candidate genes in the set of expressed genes in different human brain regions. The core function 'aba_enrich' integrates the expression of the candidate gene set (averaged across donors) and the structural information of the brain using an ontology, both provided by the Allen Brain Atlas project. 'aba_enrich' interfaces the ontology enrichment software FUNC to perform the statistical analyses.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:abaenrichment:1.4.0/cmd/bioconductor.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":36,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2018"},{"count":2,"year":"2020"},{"count":4,"year":"2019"},{"count":4,"year":"2022"},{"count":4,"year":"2023"},{"count":4,"year":"2024"},{"count":4,"year":"2026"},{"count":6,"year":"2025"},{"count":7,"year":"2021"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw392","pmcid":"PMC5048072","pmid":"27354695","ref_count":8,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2007"},{"count":1,"year":"2008"},{"count"